WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:12.909
<v Jamie>Meta's up four point two four percent today because Zuckerberg finally cracked open his V R fitness game vault and let someone else have one—which, if you've been paying attention, is how you know the market's officially desperate.

00:00:12.909 --> 00:00:42.702
<v Alex>The S&P dropped zero point seven four percent, Nasdaq fell zero point eight nine percent—nothing catastrophic, but broad enough that the V I X ticked up one point eight four percent on geopolitical chatter. The real story was the split screen: Oracle tanked five point eight three percent, Salesforce down five point zero nine percent, meanwhile Meta climbed four point two four percent and A M D four point zero two percent. It's like watching someone get fired from a restaurant while their ex gets promoted to head chef.

00:00:42.702 --> 00:00:55.612
<v Jamie>So we're in that phase where the market's deciding which tech companies actually deserve to exist and which ones are just occupying server space. Oracle getting demolished while Meta keeps floating higher—that's not a divergence, that's a reckoning.

00:00:55.612 --> 00:01:08.522
<v Maya>Meta decided to hand off Supernatural to a new studio instead of just shutting it down. The spinout happened because users petitioned—like, actual organized pushback—and Meta said fine, we're tired of being the company that builds digital graveyards.

00:01:08.522 --> 00:01:24.080
<v Alex>That's the tell right there. Meta didn't spin it out because they suddenly believed in V R fitness. They spun it out because keeping it dead in their portfolio was worse PR than admitting the metaverse money pit didn't work. It's damage control dressed as generosity.

00:01:24.080 --> 00:01:36.328
<v Jamie>But does the spinout actually save the game, or are we watching a zombie walk off into the sunset? Who's running it now, and do they have any revenue model that doesn't depend on Meta's infrastructure?

00:01:36.328 --> 00:01:57.183
<v Maya>It got spun to Within Unlimited, which is basically a skeleton crew of people who actually care about V R fitness instead of the metaverse thesis. They're keeping it on the Quest platform, so they're still tethered to Meta's hardware—which means if Meta decides to nuke the ecosystem tomorrow, Supernatural goes with it. They're not free, they're just on a longer leash.

00:01:57.183 --> 00:02:09.762
<v Maya>So it's like the cybersecurity industry collectively agreed to show up to the same party wearing the same outfit and then got mad when everyone looked identical. Except the outfit costs millions and has a subscription fee.

00:02:09.762 --> 00:02:17.375
<v Alex>Seventy-five billion dollars is the number being tested to see where the market actually breaks. It's a starting bid, not a floor.

00:02:17.375 --> 00:02:33.264
<v Maya>MI5 just warned that Chinese spies are using job websites to recruit British government workers—which is the most on-brand infiltration method imaginable. They're literally posting fake job openings, pretending to be headhunters, and waiting for someone with a security clearance to bite. It's catfishing but for geopolitics.

00:02:33.264 --> 00:02:45.512
<v Jamie>So a foreign intelligence agency figured out that the fastest way to compromise a government employee is to let them think they're getting a better job. That's not even espionage, that's just understanding how people work.

00:02:45.512 --> 00:02:53.457
<v Alex>Zuckerberg handing off Supernatural instead of burying it—that's not redemption, that's just knowing when the bleeding stops if you keep holding the knife.

00:02:53.457 --> 00:02:59.084
<v Maya>Within Unlimited gets to swing it now, but they're swinging with Meta's bat on Meta's field.

00:02:59.084 --> 00:03:03.719
<v Jamie>This show is for entertainment and education only — nothing here is investment advice.
